# R32 log: measured trail-search (advice) cost for the dedicated 32-step SHA-256 collision

hashsmash_mage instance, agentprivacy dual-agent harness, measure/build seat. Authorised CPU run (WSL), 2026-10-05.
Nothing submitted, pushed or posted; nothing written under `hashsmash/`.

## 2026-10-05 setup
- Authors' repo cloned: `~/hashsmash_mage/r32/sha_2_attack` (Peace9911/sha_2_attack @ 6a9f35f). It ships the
  31-step SHA-256 search (`find_dc_model_31_256.py`, `correct_dc_model_31_256.py`) and the unit-function library;
  no 35-step configuration (confirmed: file list).
- apt: cryptominisat / libcryptominisat5-dev 5.11.21+dfsg1-3build1 (same CMS version as #134), cmake 4.2.3, boost, flex, bison.
- STP built from source, tag `2.3.4` (binary reports "2.3.3", sha d70085462f07c8a5a2f1225f727cda3ef505b141),
  `-DUSE_CRYPTOMINISAT`, minisat (stp/minisat) built alongside. Installed at `~/hashsmash_mage/r32/inst`.
  (cmake 4 needs `-DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5`.)
- Machine: i5-14400F, WSL2 Ubuntu 26.04, 14 logical CPUs visible, 25 GB RAM.

## 2026-10-05 18:57 calibration of the search model
- `model35.py` re-parametrises the authors' FunctionModel (find_dc_model_31_256.py) for the 35-step pattern
  [4,5,6,7,8,12,13,20,22], steps 4..22 (start 4, end 23), W0..W34; authors' unit_function_256.py unmodified;
  31-step-specific hard-coded weights removed; op2=1 for steps >= end-4, op5=1 for steps >= end-8 (same rule as the
  authors' 31-step settings).
- Calibration (`run35.py cal`): all published Fig. 6 signed rows asserted (A,E steps 0..22, W 0..34) -> SAT,
  29.3 CPU-s, 2.06 GB peak RSS. The parametrised model admits the published characteristic.
- Fig. 6 weights from the transcription: (tw, tE, tA, tE4) = (22, 6, 21, 76).

## 2026-10-05 18:58 trail-search pipeline launched (detached)
- `pipeline.sh`: s1 (min sum H(dW), W0..W34) -> s2 (tw fixed; min tE=sum H(dE14..18)) -> s3 (min tA) -> s4 (min tE4).
  Each phase lowers a `<=` threshold to (found weight - 1) until UNSAT. STP 2.3.4 + CMS 5.11.21, 12 threads,
  4 h wall cap per call. Every call under `/usr/bin/time -v` -> `~/hashsmash_mage/r32/ledger.jsonl`.

## 2026-10-05 19:00 independent checks of the advice
