  - inputs: S's nabla W rows, conditioned on and priced as advice (they are already part of the attack's advice;
    our own Step-1 pattern would give a different attack needing new TAB2/q/p measurements); tE = 6 (our Step 2,
    proved optimal);
  - Step 3: our proved optimum tA = 19, then the honest upward procedure. For each tA level L = 19, 20, 21, ...,
    Step 4 runs blind and the best characteristic is checked under the exact value model (sha2_value, steps 4..22),
    continuing upward while the check fails;
  - Step 4 ladder: start <= 400, then k = best - d with d = (best - lo) / 8 initially; d halves on a timeout;
    UNSAT raises lo; it stops on a proved optimum or 3 consecutive timeouts at d = 1. 45-min caps, 7 threads, a
    fresh seed per call (seeded shuffle of the constraint order). Only bounds this run established are used: no
    76 target.
- Two lanes, foreground under background wsl.exe (2 STP processes x 7 threads = 14): lane 1 runs L = 19 then 20;
  lane 2 runs L = 21. The order of levels in the procedure is 19, 20, 21; both lanes are charged in full until the
  procedure decides.
- Stop rule: the first exact-valid characteristic of attack quality. If it equals Fig. 6, q and p are already
  measured; otherwise report.
- Wall-time estimate: per level, 6-15 ladder calls at <= 45 min plus an exact check <= 2 h, so 6-14 h per level;
  roughly 12-30 h in total with 2 lanes. Divergence check at about 24 h.

